<Page title="What Does a Luxury Bathroom Cost? (2026 Guide)" noindex description="Honest price ranges for a bathroom from Zest in Chester: what drives the cost, what is included, and how the design fee works." accent="bathrooms" eyebrow="Bathrooms — cost guide" heading="What a bathroom costs." lead="Ranges, not quotes — but real ones, from bathrooms we have designed and fitted. [All figures to be supplied by Zest.]">
  <section class="wrap section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Typical ranges</h2>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Bathroom</th><th>Sanitaryware &amp; brassware</th><th>With tiles, furniture &amp; wellness</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cloakroom</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr><tr><td>Family bathroom or en suite</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr><tr><td>Master bathroom with wet room and steam</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>What moves the number</h2>
      <p>Six things move the number, roughly in this order: the brassware house and its finish (a brushed-brass Gessi set costs several times a chrome Hansgrohe one); the sanitaryware and whether the basin is a stock ceramic or a sculpted piece; furniture, which is where Italian houses pull away; tiles and slab stone, by the square metre and by the cutting; wellness — steam, a working shower system, a sauna; and the complexity of the installation itself, which is about the existing room more than the new one.</p>
      <h2>What is included</h2>
      <p>Every figure includes the design service in full — survey, layouts, 3D visuals and the written specification — plus delivery and the project management that gets it installed. Installation is priced separately, with your installer or one of ours, because every house is different.</p>
      <h2>There is no design fee</h2>
      <p>The appointment, survey, drawings and specification are free. The price you are quoted is for the products and, if you want it, installation.</p>
    </div>
